+# YOLO drop-in contract
+
+Place a trusted, trained Ultralytics object-detection `.pt` checkpoint at
+`weights/parasite_yolo11.pt`. Install `requirements-yolo.txt`. The Detector
+automatically enables the YOLO option when this file exists; no Python edits
+are needed. Change `model.json` if you use a different filename or image size.
+Relative weight paths must remain inside this directory.
+
+The checkpoint must expose the Ultralytics detection interface and contain its
+ordered class names. Classification-only, segmentation-only, and arbitrary Torch
+state dictionaries are not equivalent formats. No COCO weights are substituted
+or downloaded. Only trusted administrator-provided checkpoints should be used.
+
+Interface: `load_yolo_model(path, file_version)` returns `(model, lock, sha256)`;
+`run_yolo_inference(model, PIL_image, confidence, iou_threshold=0.45,
+image_size=640)` returns boxes, scores, class counts, names, and an annotated PIL
+image. Loading is lazy, cached, and invalidated when file mtime or size changes.
